sting activity and surface descriptions now reflect the recovered producer/callee paths.\nfor x in m['activities']:\n a=x['class_id']\n if a=='A3':x.update(applicability='applicable',realization_summary='Log retry and snapshot recovery resynchronize peers; startup restores log/configuration from Storage and becomes follower.',unknowns=[],source_ids=['src_replication','src_snapshot_restore','src_startup','src_restore_config'])\n if a=='A4':x.update(realization_summary='Validated simple or joint changer transitions activate membership; restoration constructs equivalent ConfState and application can trigger automatic joint exit.',source_ids=['src_changer','src_restore_config','src_cfg_activation','src_applied'])\n if a=='A5':x.update(realization_summary='Ready issues eligible committed entries, tracks applying separately from applied, and processes Advance or local apply responses as caller completion signals.',source_ids=['src_log_delivery','src_log_frontiers','src_ready_accept','src_raw_advance','src_applied'])\n if a=='A6':x.update(realization_summary='Storage contract and MemoryStorage represent caller-supplied persisted history; deferred responses and term/index checked stabilization connect it to protocol support.',source_ids=['src_storage_contract','src_memory_storage','src_send','src_raw_storage_tail','src_unstable_stable'])\n if a=='A7':x['source_ids']+=['src_node_loop','src_node_propose_wait']\nm['target_profile'].update(system_boundary='Captured raft Go library, including Node serialization, RawNode state machine, quorum/configuration, log and MemoryStorage. Durable device I/O, transport delivery and client state-machine execution are caller-owned.',ownership=['RawNode caller serializes method calls; Node wraps it in a channel event loop.','Storage exposes caller-restored entries, snapshots and HardState; MemoryStorage itself is in-memory and does not establish disk durability.','Caller persists work before designated responses and applies committed entries; client completion is outside raft Propose return.'],variants=['Ready/Advance synchronous writes','AsyncStorageWrites with ordered append/apply targets','Simple and joint voter configurations with learners','Bootstrap or storage-backed restart'],source_ids=['src_raw_entry','src_node_loop','src_storage_contract','src_memory_storage','src_async_config','src_changer','src_bootstrap','src_startup'])\nm['surfaces'][0].update(disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B_RECONSTRUCT','B_CONFIG'],reason='Startup and snapshot reconstruct log/configuration through read callees; deeper caller crash-atomic storage policies remain external.',source_ids=['src_startup','src_snapshot_restore','src_restore_config','src_changer'])\nm['surfaces'][1].update(disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B_READY','B_STORAGE_FRONTIER'],reason='Traced issuance, stability eligibility and completion effects; emitted work remains distinct from completed caller work.',source_ids=['src_log_delivery','src_log_frontiers','src_raw_advance','src_applied'])\nm['surfaces'] += [dict(entry_point='raft.reset self Progress.Match initialization',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B_RESET','B_COMMIT','B_ELECT'],reason='Self Match is initialized from local lastIndex, which can include unstable history; current-term commit check is the known protection to investigate before treating Match as durable support.',source_ids=['src_reset','src_election','src_log_commit'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Ready synchronous send ordering documentation',disposition='deferred',reason='doc.go describes same-batch overlap while Ready.Messages and Ready.Entries require persistence first. A harness can comply with the stricter common subset; permissive-order responsibility remains unresolved.',source_ids=['src_usage','src_ready_contract'],high_consequence=True)]\no=m['core_overview']\no['formation']['explanation']='RawNode.Propose or serialized Node proposal handling reaches the current role. Followers forward to a known leader unless forwarding is disabled; candidates drop. The leader assigns current-term consecutive indexes, appends unstable entries, queues its own append response for persistence and broadcasts append messages anchored by previous index/term. A follower checks that anchor, appends only noncommitted conflicting suffix, bounds propagated commit to the matched extent and queues its reply through persistence. Term-filtered successful replies update peer Match. Active voter majority order statistics, or the minimum of both joint majorities, select a candidate index; leader commit advances only when that entry has its current nonzero term. Rejections, heartbeat-driven retries and snapshot fallback resynchronize lagging peers. Ready exposes committed entries only beyond the issued application frontier and blocks while a snapshot is outstanding; async delivery additionally requires locally stabilized entries. Caller application is reported by Advance or local apply response, advancing applied and freeing budget. Client proposal return is only admission/Step outcome and can precede or never lead to commitment.'\no['formation']['behavior_ids']+=['B_REPLICATION_SEND','B_STORAGE_FRONTIER','B_NODE_OWNER']\no['formation']['source_ids']+=['src_replication','src_replication_retry','src_log_delivery','src_log_frontiers','src_raw_advance','src_applied','src_node_loop','src_node_propose_wait']\no['context']['explanation']+=' Startup reconstructs log bounds and configuration from caller Storage, loads saved term/vote/commit and becomes follower. Snapshot restoration rejects obsolete or ineligible snapshots, fast-forwards a matching committed boundary, or installs snapshot history and configuration; a pending snapshot prevents promotion. Configuration activation uses validated simple changes or joint enter/leave, preserves progress for retained peers, initializes new progress at zero and handles configured leader removal. Application progress can initiate automatic joint exit.'\no['context']['behavior_ids']+=['B_RECONSTRUCT','B_CONFIG']\no['context']['source_ids']+=['src_startup','src_snapshot_restore','src_changer','src_restore_config','src_log_recover','src_applied']\no['connection']['explanation']='Term/role reset discards votes, peer progress and safe-read acknowledgment tracker while preserving local log and committed frontier. Self progress is initialized from local lastIndex, including potentially unstable inherited entries, so Match must not be equated with a fresh durable acknowledgment. Leader formation appends a current-term empty entry; commit requires the selected entry term to equal the leader term, preventing the old self frontier alone from authorizing new-term commitment. Active membership changes reinterpret retained progress and can re-evaluate commit; new peers begin Match=0. Stale-term replies do not advance leader support or stabilize entries. Local append completion additionally matches entry term/index; a later current-term append message can reconfirm outstanding writes. Committed state and application acknowledgments survive term changes: apply responses are term zero, snapshot completion can be processed despite stale term, and applied uses a monotonic maximum. Pending pre-commit read requests survive reset but enter the new read-only mechanism only after current-term commitment; existing safe-read acknowledgment state is reset. Recovery starts as follower with caller-supplied persisted prefix and configuration, not restored leadership.'\no['connection']['behavior_ids']+=['B_STORAGE_FRONTIER','B_RECONSTRUCT','B_READ_CONTEXT']\no['connection']['source_ids']+=['src_startup','src_changer','src_log_recover','src_log_delivery','src_raw_storage_tail','src_applied','src_pending_reads','src_read_tracker']\no.update(status='usable',core_gaps=[],open_details=['Synchronous documentation overlap wording remains unresolved; persist-before-send is the explicit Ready field contract and common safe caller policy.','Lease-read timing assumptions and full read response construction remain open; safe-read context production/consumption is traced only to explain old pending work.','Caller crash atomicity, durable storage implementations beyond MemoryStorage, and application snapshot coordination are external boundaries requiring a concrete harness policy for a future question.'],rationale='Representative proposal-to-application and authority/recovery paths now connect through actual producers, consumers, eligibility and persistence handoffs. Usability is a sourced navigation judgment, not a safety proof or full variant coverage.')\nchanges={}\n# Each modified existing semantic object is explicitly attributed.\nfor collection,key in [('behaviors','id'),('facts','id'),('activities','class_id')]:\n oldby={x[key]:x for x in old[collection]}\n for x in m[collection]:\n  if x[key] in oldby and x\"'!=oldby[x[key]]:\n   ids=[i for i in x.get('\"'source_ids',[]) if i in {s['id'] for s in sources}]\n   if not ids:ids=['src_startup']\n   impact='meaning' if x[key]=='F_MATCH' else ('dependency' if x[key]=='B_RESET' else 'clarification')\n   changes[x[key]]=dict(impact=impact,source_ids=ids,rationale='Recovered actual producers/callees and replaced the explicitly recorded reading gap. For F_MATCH and B_RESET, explicitly include self initialization: local Match is not always fresh durable acknowledgment.',preserves='No Candidate or Unit exists. Other facts retain distinct queue, commitment and leadership meanings; no execution observations or requirements are changed.',challenges={})\nchanges['core_overview']=dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=['src_startup','src_replication','src_changer','src_log_delivery','src_raw_advance','src_node_loop'],rationale='Close the three recorded backbone gaps with actual recovery, configuration, transmission and completion callees; retain specific interface and variant details.',preserves='The map remains an implementation explanation, without correctness or coverage conclusion.',challenges={})\njson.dump(m,open('audit-map.json','w'),indent=2)\ns=dict(action='research',rationale='Complete the sourced two-core backbone and correct self Match semantics before selecting a focused question.',sources=sources,map_path='audit-map.json',map_changes=changes,feedback=dict(ref_ids=[s['id'] for s in sources]+['src_reset','src_log_commit'],answered='Traced actual reconstruction, simple/joint configuration producers, append/snapshot retries, Node serialization, issuance and application completion. The overview is now usable for navigation. Corrected F_MATCH: reset initializes self Match from lastIndex even when history remains unstable; current-term commit matching and delayed new-entry self acknowledgments are distinct protections. Retained documented synchronous ordering discrepancy and caller durability/application boundaries. No implementation execution or property conclusion is asserted.',remaining=['Select a local discriminator over self-progress initialization and current-term commitment, or term-qualified storage stabilization feeding application eligibility.','Before executing, define a legal public entry and caller storage policy; the current-term guard alone is not an independent normative obligation.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The smallest useful next discriminator is whether inherited self Match can be consumed to commit prior-term history before any current-term entry obtains qualified support. First compare the known current-term guard and deferred self acknowledgment with an actual producer history; this may yield a sourced explanation without an execution. If explained, term-qualified append completion is an independent mapped consumer boundary.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 complete_map.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(m